+
+## UBU-D0378: Restricted-attention acknowledgments bind controller outcomes
+
+**Status:** Accepted → DESIGN.md §21.1.2. Partially answers `UBU-Q0128` subquestions 9, 12 and 18; refines `UBU-D0310` under `UBU-D0359` and `UBU-D0365` without widening the initial envelope.
+
+Adopt `audio-feedback/1` for controller-rendered terminal acknowledgments. Fixed English phrases distinguish a durably retained review artifact, a failed or uncertain save, a confirmed scoped media effect, a failed or unsent control and an uncertain effect. Model intent, confidence, dispatch acceptance and coincident playback state cannot select a success phrase. Saving evidence of a media attempt cannot establish that attempt's effect.
+
+Allow at most one terminal speech attempt per original turn. Preflight the complete phrase against remaining byte, rendered-speech and elapsed limits, then recheck current bindings and output disclosure before release. Suppress unavailable output without shortening qualifications, replaying speech or renewing the turn. Pause/Stop/Silence remains immediate and receives no spoken acknowledgment under this profile.
+
+Link outcome evidence, template and output disposition through existing minimized audit records; completed output proves neither hearing nor comprehension. Require §21.1.2's storage-failure, unknown-effect, duplicate, interruption and rendering-boundary fixtures, plus the existing comprehension trials. This specifies rendering behavior, not implementation, measured usability or a driving-safety result. Both v1 schemas and MVP-release scope remain unchanged; `UBU-Q0128` stays Open for measured profiles and its other remaining slices.
+
+---
